       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Single doses are typically no more than 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
